  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Define day metadata once for your application through a shared provider, or add entries directly to an individual calendar or picker. When both sources supply metadata for the same date, the local entry controls the indicator and whether the day is disabled. Tooltips show local content first, followed by provider content and any enabled calendar event details.\n\nUse `ShowDayMetadata` to turn off all metadata effects on a control, or use `ShowDayMetadataIndicators` and `ShowDayMetadataToolTips` to hide either visual separately. This lets a birthday picker or a grid editor use the same calendar without applying shared metadata.\n\n**Breaking change:** `DayMetadata` now accepts `IList<CalendarDayInfo>` in place of `IDictionary<DateTime, CalendarDayInfo>`. Move each dictionary key to the entry's `Date` property and update any bindings that supply a dictionary.\n\n\nCreate day metadata with `new CalendarDayInfo(date)`. Calendars and pickers now reflect edits to existing local entries automatically, including changes to tooltips, indicators, and disabled states. Changing an entry's date updates both the old and new day.\n\nAfter changing data from a shared provider, call `CalendarDayMetadataConfiguration.Refresh()` to reload it.\n\nDayIndicator2 has been removed from Automation's internal and output templates, and tests or templates that reference it should use DayIndicator1.",
